  "name": "Force-on-force experimental model v2 (weapons and ammunition)",
  "notes": [
    "Experimental parameters for a constructive simulation prototype. They are not validated military detection or lethality data.",
    "Detection structure (cycles across the target, the target transfer probability function, an exponential search-time law, Koschmieder haze) follows the published target-acquisition literature; every value applied to the naked eye, and every contrast, clutter and attention factor, is an experimental assumption (docs/behavior-lab/force-on-force/02-detection-research.md).",
    "Weapon, suppression, effectiveness and termination values are illustrative and chosen to give interpretable engagements, not tuned for either side.",
    "Weapons (v2): feeds, basic loads, doctrinal sustained and rapid rates and burst lengths from FM 3-22.9 (M16A4), FM 3-22.68 (M249) and FM 3-22.31 (M203); reload times, the burst-round weight, the M203 basic load and its incapacitation falloff are modelling assumptions (docs/behavior-lab/force-on-force/06-weapons-and-ammunition.md)."
  ],
